<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: AIB 1996 pre-tax profit rises 13 pct.</title>
<headline>AIB 1996 pre-tax profit rises 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  38.4		 vs 34.2</p>
<p> Dividend  (pence)	  9.05		 vs 7.7</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)   15.0		 vs 12.9</p>
<p> Pretax profit		420.8		vs 372.6</p>
<p> Operating profit	   410.8		vs 370.1</p>
<p> Bad debt provision	 52.1		 vs 52.5</p>
<p> Net interest income	837.1		vs 796.4</p>
<p> Total operating income  1,303.6	     vs 1,197.7</p>
<p> Total operating expenses 840.4		vs 774.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits of 412.5 million to 413.0 million Irish pounds.</p>
<p>Full company name - Allied Irish Banks Plc.</p>
</text>
